### Create One Time Code (CREATED)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/otc
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 123,
  "bankId": 45,
  "availableLoanLimit": 120000,
  "expiryMinutes": 59
}

### Get One Time Code by id
GET http://localhost:8080/api/otc/1

### Activate One Time Code (CREATED -> ACTIVE)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/otc/1/activate

### Use One Time Code (ACTIVE -> USED) (single-use)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/otc/1/use
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 5000
}

### Cancel One Time Code (CREATED/ACTIVE -> CANCELLED)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/otc/1/cancel

### Notes
# - If pass is expired (validTo < now) and state is CREATED/ACTIVE, it auto-moves to CANCELLED.
# - If you see 409 Conflict on create, it was a rare code collision; retry (generator retries internally too).
